        }
      ],
      "answer": "C",
      "answer_index": 2,
      "analysis_html": "<div class=\"math-tex math-block\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}P\\{X\\geq 10\\} &amp;= 1-P\\{X&lt;10\\} \\ = 1-(1-e^{-1/5\\times 10})=e^{-2},\\\\ \\therefore P\\{Y=k\\} &amp;= C_2^k(e^{-2})^k(1-e^{-2})^{5-k},\\, k=0,\\,1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,4,\\,5,\\\\ P\\{Y\\geq 1\\} &amp;= 1-(1-e^{-2})^5 \\approx 0.5167.\\end{aligned}\">\\begin{aligned}P\\{X\\geq 10\\} &amp;= 1-P\\{X&lt;10\\} \\ = 1-(1-e^{-1/5\\times 10})=e^{-2},\\\\ \\therefore P\\{Y=k\\} &amp;= C_2^k(e^{-2})^k(1-e^{-2})^{5-k},\\, k=0,\\,1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,4,\\,5,\\\\ P\\{Y\\geq 1\\} &amp;= 1-(1-e^{-2})^5 \\approx 0.5167.\\end{aligned}</div>"
